E331                             ; pesc: the escapes of "$". A = the character after the "/", 60h to 7Eh, and
E331                             ; the carry is clear. Each returns into the loop.
E331                             ;    /a-/z   print the variable, as "#" does
E331                             ;    /{      clear the screen, the cursor to the top left
E331                             ;    /}      clear from the cursor to the end of the line
E331                             ;    /|  /`  show the cursor, hide it
E331                             ;    /~      ( row col addr -- addr ): the cursor to that row and column,
E331                             ;            from 0. The two cells under the string's address go.
E331                             ; A - 7Bh sorts them: 00bbIDAsIHwgMSwg 2, ~ 3 with the carry set, and ` E5h, a-z
E331                             ; E6h-FFh with it clear.
E331                          IF   1-ANSI   
E331                             ; With ANSI = 0 the machine's routines do the work.
